**Headline verdicts the review will report.**

- **Explicit causality: largely delivered.** No registry, host-owned dispatch, per-attachment identities on every event, caller-owned cadence, and a bounded pre-accept handoff through streams. Three leaks: the JVM adapter blocks inside a contractually non-blocking `append!`, the transport host edges deposit REPL-namespaced error codes, and `serving/stop!` leaves pre-accept sockets open.
